Z||000000||turbo86se||12-11-1999||12:26 AM||||<BR>Hi everyone, I just got a Pioneer DEH 45 CD player from a fellow Fiero owner in CA, and I made my first attempt to install it. First, I made all the connections to the back of the CD player to the car's wiring, and nothing worked. No power. There is a two wire connector that isn't hooked up to anything at this point(orange and black). So with the help of the original owner, he said to wire the loose battery wire to the orange wire on the two wire connector. OK, I get power now, and the CD player works and sounds great!  Now, the factory subwoofer doesn't work. Just for trial, I re-attached the factory radio, and the sub works fine. The sub works without the orange and black wire hooked up to anything. Any ideas on what I did wrong? Or do I need some kind of special adapter for the radio and sub to work on the new radio? Any help is greatly appreciated!  Thanks!! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||12-11-1999||01:03 AM||||The factory sub amp gets power from the stock radio. You will need to put a key hot power to the pink wire to power the amp.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||12-11-1999||03:33 AM||||Thanks Tom, I had a feeling it would be something simple. How would I wire it up? What would be the easiest way to give the amp the power? I've also heard there's a special adapter I can get at Crutchfield, does this work the same way? Thanks again,||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||12-11-1999||12:11 PM||||uh oh, I just went out to check out the pink wire, and there's two! Exactly the same color, right on top of another in the harness!  Help!||||reg||1
